&lt;br /&gt;
The 2026 Annual Regional High School Art Show is now on display at Pacific Northwest University of Medical Sciences, showcasing 85 works of art created by talented high school students from 7 high schools across five South Central Washington school districts. Coordinated by Educational Service District 105, the exhibit will be open to the public &lt;strong&gt;March 9, 2026 through March 19, 2026.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); color:rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size:11pt"&gt;This year&rsquo;s juried show features artwork from the Yakima, Kittitas, Royal, Wapato, Granger and Grandview school districts. Fifteen Judges Choice awards, five ESD105&amp;nbsp; Awards, and two ESD Board of Director&rsquo;s Awards will be presented, celebrating exceptional creativity and craftsmanship. The ESD105 Board of Director&rsquo;s awards will find a permanent place in the ESD105 Board of Director&rsquo;s Art Gallery on the main campus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); color:rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size:11pt"&gt;Central Washington University (CWU) will award scholarships to selected student artists in recognition of their outstanding work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p dir="ltr"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255); color:rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size:11pt"&gt;Following the Awards Presentation students and guests will gather for&amp;nbsp; The Art Gallery Walk to view the exhibit and celebrate our young artists creativity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

